commodore-900-coh-kernel3
==========================

The COHERENT 3-series kernel for the Commodore 900 (Zilog Z8001): the
3.2-derived portable core plus the Z8001 machine layer (os/sys), the hi-res
console driver (os/hrtty), the kernel-class headers, and the host build that
links, tests and packages them.

`kernel3` names a DERIVATION, not a product version: this source descends
from the COHERENT 3.x line, as opposed to the separate 0.7-derived kernel
that remains in commodore-900-coherent (src/kernel) pending its own decision.
The two share no source and are not two versions of one codebase.

Building
--------

    make deps        # clone commodore-900-toolchain and commodore-900-kboot
                      # beside this repository (see DEPS)
    make kernel       # link os/hostbuild/kobj/kernel.out
    make drivers      # the loadable console drivers, bound to that kernel
    make kernel-dist  # the packaged deliverable (see os/hostbuild/pack-kernel.sh)
    make kernel-headers
    make check-stamps
    make help

`make deps` places the two checkouts DEPS names as siblings of this
repository (or inside a `repos/` directory beside it); set C900_TOOLCHAIN or
C900_KBOOT to point at checkouts elsewhere. See DEPS for what each edge is
for and why there is no `emu` or `lexicon` row here.

What this repository does not contain
--------------------------------------

No image assembly, no media/partition descriptors, and no userland: this
repository links a kernel and its drivers, and packages them for a consumer
(the dist repository) to stage onto a disk alongside a userland package. It
depends on commodore-900-toolchain for the Z8001 compiler, assembler and
linker, and on commodore-900-kboot for the loader-to-kernel handoff header
(include/bootinfo.h) it compiles in.

History
-------

Split from commodore-900-coherent by TASK-288, with git-filter-repo, so
`git log --follow` on a file under os/sys or os/hrtty reaches back through
that repository's history rather than starting fresh.

See LICENSE and NOTICE for what this source is and who holds copyright over
it.
